-- title:
--   Points of the character closure are L-valued characters of S
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a Noetherian principal ideal domain with fraction field $F$, let $A$ be a commutative, cocommutative Hopf $O$-algebra that is finite and free as an $O$-module, and let $L$ be a field which is an $F$-algebra and an $O$-algebra compatibly. The assertion is the existence of a rule $\chi$ which, for every submonoid $S$ of the convolution monoid of $F$-algebra maps $F\otimes_O A\to L$ with $S$ finite, and given (i) that an element of $(F\otimes_O A/I_S)\otimes_F(F\otimes_O A/I_S)$ killed by all the maps [`HopfAlgebra.evalPair`](def/HopfAlgebra_CharacterClosure.html#L35) attached to pairs $\nu,\nu'$ of points lying in $S$ is zero, where $I_S$ is the vanishing ideal of those points, (ii) that for each such $\nu$ there is another point $\nu'$ of $S$ with $\nu'=\nu\circ(\text{antipode})$ as $F$-linear maps, and (iii) that [`HopfAlgebra.evalQuot S`](def/HopfAlgebra_CharacterClosure.html#L66) : $L\otimes_F(F\otimes_O A/I_S)\to (S\to L)$ is bijective, produces a bijection between the convolution-monoid type of $O$-algebra maps from the character closure $E_S$ — the $O$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{CartierDual}\,O\,A$ of those $g$ with $1\otimes g$ in the $F$-subalgebra of $F\otimes_O\mathrm{CartierDual}\,O\,A$ generated by the functionals annihilating $I_S$ — to $L$, and the monoid homomorphisms $S\to L$. Three compatibilities are asserted: $\chi_S$ is multiplicative for the convolution products whenever that generic-fibre character algebra is comultiplication- and antipode-stable, so that $E_S$ carries the Hopf $O$-algebra structure given by [`closureHopfAlgebra`](def/FiniteFlat_ClosureHopfAlgebra.html#L299); for $\sigma\in\mathrm{Aut}_F(L)$ and points $\nu,\nu'$ of $S$ with $\nu'=\sigma\circ\nu$, one has $\chi_S(\sigma\circ\psi)(\nu')=\sigma(\chi_S(\psi)(\nu))$; and for $S\le S'$ both satisfying the hypotheses, restricting a point of $E_{S'}$ along the inclusion $E_S\subseteq E_{S'}$ and applying $\chi_S$ agrees at $\nu\in S$ with $\chi_{S'}$ of the point evaluated at the image of $\nu$ in $S'$.
--
--   This is the Cartier-duality dictionary "points of the dual are characters" in the form needed for the integral models $E_S$ of the Cartier duals of the finite subgroup schemes cut out by finite groups $S$ of generic-fibre points, together with its functoriality in $S$ and its $\mathrm{Aut}(L/F)$-equivariance. It is used in the analysis of finite flat Hopf models along admissible chains, where trivial inertia action on the points of the dual is converted into a cyclotomic action on $S$.
